/-!
# Descent of étale sheaves along a morphism with a representable covering refinement

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` and `π : X' ⟶ X` be morphisms of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S` contained
in a big fppf site `B`, and suppose the *composite* `π ≫ f` is representable by schemes and is
surjective and integral, surjective and proper, or surjective and flat and locally of finite
presentation. Then spaces-étale sheaves on `Y` are equivalent to descent data for the singleton
family `{X ⟶ Y}`, even though `f` itself carries none of those hypotheses. This is
**Stacks 0GFV**.

The source proof is one sentence: it is the formal consequence of Stacks 0GFU — the same
statement when the morphism carrying the hypotheses *is* the morphism of the descent problem —
and Stacks 0GEA, the refinement principle that descent along a family follows from descent along
a family refining it. The family `{X' ⟶ Y}` refines `{X ⟶ Y}` through `π`, which is how `π`
enters.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsSurjectiveIntegralProperOrFlatLfp`: the three-way alternative on a
  morphism of algebraic spaces used by Stacks 0GFU, 0GFV and 0GFW — surjective and integral, or
  surjective and proper, or surjective and flat and locally of finite presentation.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.isEquivalence_toDescentData_of_homOver`: **Stacks 0GEA at an
  arbitrary pseudofunctor**, rather than only at the pullback pseudofunctor of a fibred category;
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsSurjectiveIntegralProperOrFlatLfp.of_isPullback`: that alternative
  is stable under base change;
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isEquivalence_toDescentData_singleton_of_representable_comp`:
  **Stacks 0GFV** for the pseudofunctor of spaces-étale inverse images, granted the conclusion of
  Stacks 0GFU.

## Implementation notes

**What is granted.** Stacks 0GFU is not available in this library: no declaration carries the
attribute `@[stacks 0GFU]`. Its conclusion is therefore taken as the single explicitly named
hypothesis `h0GFU` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isEquivalence_toDescentData_singleton_of_representable_comp`, in its
universally quantified form — for *every* morphism of algebraic spaces over `S` which is
representable by schemes and satisfies
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsSurjectiveIntegralProperOrFlatLfp`, spaces-étale sheaves on its target
are equivalent to descent data for the singleton family it generates. The grant is instantiated
three times: at `π ≫ f` itself, and at the base changes of `π ≫ f` along `f` and along
`X ×_Y X ⟶ Y`, which are the two local hypotheses of Stacks 0GEA.

The grant is *not* this statement's own conclusion in disguise. Universally quantified, this
statement says: for all `f` and all `π`, if `π ≫ f` is representable and satisfies the
alternative, then descent holds along `f`. The grant is its special case `π = 𝟙 X`, in which the
morphism carrying the hypotheses coincides with the morphism of the descent problem. The
implication runs only that way: the grant follows from the conclusion by taking `π = 𝟙 X`, while
recovering the conclusion from the grant requires the refinement principle, because `f` itself
need be neither representable nor surjective — it is `π ≫ f` that is, and no instance of the
grant has `f` in the hypothesis position.

**What is proved rather than granted.** The Stacks 0GEA step is proved. The library's form
`CategoryTheory.Functor.isEquivalence_toFamilyDescentDatum_of_homOver` of
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Descent.OfRefinement` is stated for the pullback pseudofunctor
of a fibred category, and the pseudofunctor of spaces-étale inverse images is not presented that
way, so the statement is redone here for an arbitrary pseudofunctor. It is assembled from exactly
the general-pseudofunctor lemmas that proof consumes, all of them available:
`CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.DescentData.nonempty_fullyFaithful_pullFunctor` for the local full
faithfulness of the refinement functor, `CategoryTheory.PreZeroHypercover.ofArrows_pullback₁` to
identify the sieve generated by a base changed family,
`CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.isSeparatedFor_presheafHom_of_faithful` for the separatedness over
the fibre products, and Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.DescentData.toDescentDataCompPullFunctorIso` for the two-out-of-
three argument. Nothing in that step is assumed.

**The hypotheses the refinement step asks for are discharged, not carried.** Stacks 0GEA needs
the fibre products `X ×_Y X`, `X ×_Y X'` and `X ×_Y X ×_Y X'`; all three exist, by the global
instance `AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpaces.hasPullbacks` of Stacks 02X2. Its two local
hypotheses are instances of the grant at base changes of `π ≫ f`, which needs representability
and the three-way alternative to be stable under base change; both are available, the first as
`CategoryTheory.Functor.relativelyRepresentable.isStableUnderBaseChange` and the second as
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsSurjectiveIntegralProperOrFlatLfp.of_isPullback`, proved here from
Stacks 03MH, 03ZS, 04WP, 03MO and 03XR.

**The shape of the conclusion.** As in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Topologies.SpacesEtaleGlobalDescent` and
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Topologies.SpacesEtaleDescentEtaleLocal`, the descent
problem is phrased for `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.spacesEtalePseudofunctor`, the pseudofunctor of
spaces-étale inverse images on the category of all algebraic spaces over `S`, and "descent data
for `{X ⟶ Y}`" is `CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.toDescentData` at the singleton family indexed
by `Unit`. The source phrases it for the small étale topoi, which are the same topoi by
Stacks 03G1.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GFV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GFV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GFU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GFU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GEA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GEA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GFS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GFS)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe w' w t' t v' v u' u

namespace CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C]

/-- **Stacks 0GEA at an arbitrary pseudofunctor.**
Let `𝒱 = {V j ⟶ U} ⟶ 𝒰 = {U i ⟶ U}` be a morphism of families of morphisms with fixed target
given by `𝟙 U`, a reindexing and morphisms `V j ⟶ U (s₀ j)`, and let `F` be a pseudofunctor into
`Cat`. Assume that the fibre products `U i₁ ×_U U i₂`, `U i ×_U V j` and `U i₁ ×_U U i₂ ×_U V j`
exist, that `F U ⟶ DD(𝒱)` is an equivalence, that `F (U i) ⟶ DD(𝒱_i)` is fully faithful for
every `i`, and that `F (U i₁ ×_U U i₂) ⟶ DD(𝒱_{i₁i₂})` is faithful for every `i₁, i₂`, where
`𝒱_i` and `𝒱_{i₁i₂}` are the base changes of `𝒱`. Then `F U ⟶ DD(𝒰)` is an equivalence.

`CategoryTheory.Functor.isEquivalence_toFamilyDescentDatum_of_homOver` is this statement for the
pullback pseudofunctor of a fibred category; the proof is the same, since every lemma it uses
holds at an arbitrary pseudofunctor. -/
theorem isEquivalence_toDescentData_of_homOver
    (F : Pseudofunctor (LocallyDiscrete Cᵒᵖ) Cat.{v', u'}) {U : C}
    {𝒰 : PreZeroHypercover.{w} U} {𝒱 : PreZeroHypercover.{w'} U} (Φ : 𝒱.HomOver 𝒰 (𝟙 U))
    [∀ i₁ i₂, HasPullback (𝒰.f i₁) (𝒰.f i₂)]
    [∀ i j, HasPullback (𝒰.f i) (𝒱.f j)]
    [∀ i₁ i₂ j, HasPullback (pullback.fst (𝒰.f i₁) (𝒰.f i₂) ≫ 𝒰.f i₁) (𝒱.f j)]
    (h₂ : (F.toDescentData 𝒱.f).IsEquivalence)
    (h₃ : ∀ i, Nonempty (F.toDescentData (𝒱.pullback₁ (𝒰.f i)).f).FullyFaithful)
    (h₄ : ∀ i₁ i₂, (F.toDescentData
      (𝒱.pullback₁ (pullback.fst (𝒰.f i₁) (𝒰.f i₂) ≫ 𝒰.f i₁)).f).Faithful) :
    (F.toDescentData 𝒰.f).IsEquivalence := by
  have w : ∀ j, Φ.h₀ j ≫ 𝒰.f (Φ.s₀ j) = 𝒱.f j :=
    fun j ↦ (Φ.w₀ j).trans (Category.comp_id _)
  have H₃ : ∀ (i : 𝒰.I₀) (M N : F.obj (.mk (op (𝒰.X i)))),
      Presieve.IsSheafFor (F.presheafHom M N)
        (DescentData.refSieve 𝒱.f (𝟙 (𝒰.X i)) (𝒰.f i)).arrows := by
    intro i M N
    have hpre : F.IsPrestackFor
        (Sieve.pullback (𝒰.f i) (Sieve.ofArrows 𝒱.X 𝒱.f)).arrows := by
      rw [← 𝒱.ofArrows_pullback₁ (𝒰.f i), Sieve.ofArrows, IsPrestackFor_generate_iff,
        isPrestackFor_ofArrows_iff]
      exact h₃ i
    exact (F.isPrestackFor_iff_isSheafFor' _).1 hpre M N (𝟙 _)
  have H₄ : ∀ (i₁ i₂ : 𝒰.I₀) (M N : F.obj (.mk (op (𝒰.X i₁)))),
      Presieve.IsSeparatedFor (F.presheafHom M N)
        (DescentData.refSieve 𝒱.f (pullback.fst (𝒰.f i₁) (𝒰.f i₂))
          (pullback.fst (𝒰.f i₁) (𝒰.f i₂) ≫ 𝒰.f i₁)).arrows := by
    intro i₁ i₂ M N
    have := h₄ i₁ i₂
    have h := isSeparatedFor_presheafHom_of_faithful (F := F)
      (𝒱.pullback₁ (pullback.fst (𝒰.f i₁) (𝒰.f i₂) ≫ 𝒰.f i₁)).f
      (pullback.fst (𝒰.f i₁) (𝒰.f i₂)) M N
    rwa [𝒱.ofArrows_pullback₁] at h
  obtain ⟨hff⟩ := DescentData.nonempty_fullyFaithful_pullFunctor
    (F := F) (f := 𝒰.f) (f' := 𝒱.f) (α := Φ.s₀) (p' := Φ.h₀) w
    (fun _ _ i ↦ H₃ i _ _) (fun i₁ i₂ ↦ .ofHasPullback _ _) (fun _ _ i₁ i₂ ↦ H₄ i₁ i₂ _ _)
  have := hff.full
  have := hff.faithful
  have := h₂
  set G := DescentData.pullFunctor F (f := 𝒰.f) (p := 𝟙 _) (f' := 𝒱.f) (p' := Φ.h₀)
    (DescentData.w_comp_id w)
  have e : F.toDescentData 𝒰.f ⋙ G ≅ F.toDescentData 𝒱.f :=
    DescentData.toDescentDataCompPullFunctorIso _ _ ≪≫
      Functor.isoWhiskerRight (Cat.Hom.toNatIso (F.mapId _)) _ ≪≫ Functor.leftUnitor _
  have := Functor.Faithful.of_comp_iso e
  have := Functor.Full.of_comp_faithful_iso e
  have : (F.toDescentData 𝒰.f ⋙ G).IsEquivalence := Functor.isEquivalence_of_iso e.symm
  have := Functor.essSurj_of_comp_fully_faithful (F.toDescentData 𝒰.f) G
  exact { }

end CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- The three-way alternative on a morphism of algebraic spaces over `S` which Stacks 0GFU,
0GFV and 0GFW ask for: it is surjective and integral, or surjective and proper, or surjective
and flat and locally of finite presentation. The three cases are alternatives, not simultaneous
assumptions. -/
abbrev IsSurjectiveIntegralProperOrFlatLfp {X Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} (f : X ⟶ Y) : Prop :=
  (IsSurjective B S hS f.hom ∧ IsIntegralHom B S hS f.hom) ∨
    (IsSurjective B S hS f.hom ∧ IsProper B S hS f.hom) ∨
    (IsSurjective B S hS f.hom ∧ IsFlat B S hS f.hom ∧
      IsLocallyOfFinitePresentation B S hS f.hom)

/-- Each of the three alternatives of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsSurjectiveIntegralProperOrFlatLfp` is preserved by arbitrary base
change, so the alternative itself is: surjectivity by Stacks 03MH, integrality by Stacks 03ZS,
properness by Stacks 04WP, flatness by Stacks 03MO and being locally of finite presentation by
Stacks 03XR. -/
theorem IsSurjectiveIntegralProperOrFlatLfp.of_isPullback
    {W X Y Z : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} {p : W ⟶ Z} {q : W ⟶ X} {g : Z ⟶ Y} {f : X ⟶ Y}
    (sq : IsPullback p q g f) (hg : IsSurjectiveIntegralProperOrFlatLfp B S hS g) :
    IsSurjectiveIntegralProperOrFlatLfp B S hS q := by
  have sqh : IsPullback p.hom q.hom g.hom f.hom := AlgebraicSpaces.isPullback_hom _ _ _ sq
  rcases hg with ⟨hs, hi⟩ | ⟨hs, hp⟩ | ⟨hs, hfl, hlfp⟩
  · exact .inl ⟨isSurjective_of_isPullback B S hS sq hs,
      isIntegralHom_of_isPullback B S hS sqh hi⟩
  · exact .inr (.inl ⟨isSurjective_of_isPullback B S hS sq hs,
      (isProper_isStableUnderBaseChange B S hS).of_isPullback sq hp⟩)
  · exact .inr (.inr ⟨isSurjective_of_isPullback B S hS sq hs,
      (isFlat_isStableUnderBaseChange B S hS).of_isPullback sq hfl,
      (isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_isStableUnderBaseChange B S hS).of_isPullback sq hlfp⟩)

/-- **Stacks 0GFV for the pseudofunctor of spaces-étale inverse images.** Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a
morphism of algebraic spaces over `S` and let `π : X' ⟶ X` be a morphism of algebraic spaces.
If the composite `π ≫ f` is representable by schemes and is surjective and integral, surjective
and proper, or surjective and flat and locally of finite presentation, then spaces-étale sheaves
on `Y` are equivalent, via the canonical descent datum, to descent data for the singleton family
`{X ⟶ Y}`. No hypothesis is placed on `f` itself.

The conclusion of Stacks 0GFU is granted as `h0GFU`; see the implementation notes of the file. -/
@[stacks 0GFV "granted `h0GFU`, the conclusion of Stacks 0GFU: that for EVERY morphism of \
algebraic spaces over `S` which is representable by schemes and is surjective and integral, \
surjective and proper, or surjective and flat and locally of finite presentation, spaces-étale \
sheaves on its target are equivalent to descent data for the singleton family it generates. \
That is the special case `π = 𝟙 X` of this statement, in which the morphism carrying the \
hypotheses is the morphism of the descent problem itself, so it is NOT the universally \
quantified form of this conclusion: this conclusion asks for descent along `f` while the \
hypotheses are carried by `π ≫ f`, and `f` itself is neither representable nor surjective in \
any instance of the grant. The implication runs one way only — the grant is an instance of \
this conclusion, and getting this conclusion back out of the grant is exactly the refinement \
step. That step, Stacks 0GEA, is proved and not granted: \
`CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.isEquivalence_toDescentData_of_homOver` of this file restates the \
library's `CategoryTheory.Functor.isEquivalence_toFamilyDescentDatum_of_homOver` at an arbitrary \
pseudofunctor, and its fibre-product and base-change obligations are discharged here"]
theorem isEquivalence_toDescentData_singleton_of_representable_comp
    (h0GFU : ∀ {X₀ Y₀ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} (f₀ : X₀ ⟶ Y₀),
      yoneda.relativelyRepresentable f₀.hom →
      IsSurjectiveIntegralProperOrFlatLfp B S hS f₀ →
      ((spacesEtalePseudofunctor B S hS).toDescentData
        (fun _ : Unit => f₀)).IsEquivalence)
    {X' X Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} (π : X' ⟶ X) (f : X ⟶ Y)
    (hrep : yoneda.relativelyRepresentable (π ≫ f).hom)
    (hcov : IsSurjectiveIntegralProperOrFlatLfp B S hS (π ≫ f)) :
    ((spacesEtalePseudofunctor B S hS).toDescentData
      (fun _ : Unit => f)).IsEquivalence := by
  have key : ∀ {Z : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} (q : Z ⟶ Y),
      ((spacesEtalePseudofunctor B S hS).toDescentData
        (fun _ : Unit => pullback.fst q (π ≫ f))).IsEquivalence := by
    intro Z q
    have sq := (IsPullback.of_hasPullback q (π ≫ f)).flip
    exact h0GFU _ ((Functor.relativelyRepresentable.isStableUnderBaseChange yoneda).of_isPullback
      (AlgebraicSpaces.isPullback_hom _ _ _ sq) hrep)
      (IsSurjectiveIntegralProperOrFlatLfp.of_isPullback B S hS sq hcov)
  refine Pseudofunctor.isEquivalence_toDescentData_of_homOver
    (spacesEtalePseudofunctor B S hS)
    (𝒰 := ⟨Unit, fun _ => X, fun _ => f⟩) (𝒱 := ⟨Unit, fun _ => X', fun _ => π ≫ f⟩)
    { s₀ := fun _ => (), h₀ := fun _ => π, w₀ := fun _ => by simp } ?_ ?_ ?_
  · exact h0GFU (π ≫ f) hrep hcov
  · intro i
    have := key f
    change Nonempty ((spacesEtalePseudofunctor B S hS).toDescentData
      (fun _ : Unit => pullback.fst f (π ≫ f))).FullyFaithful
    exact ⟨.ofFullyFaithful _⟩
  · intro i₁ i₂
    have := key (pullback.fst f f ≫ f)
    change ((spacesEtalePseudofunctor B S hS).toDescentData
      (fun _ : Unit => pullback.fst (pullback.fst f f ≫ f) (π ≫ f))).Faithful
    infer_instance

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
